## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to translate a performance problem into a concrete, actionable plan with beginner-level scope.

## Key Concepts

- Telemetry-driven optimization
- Safe experiments with feature flags
- Incident response basics
- Stakeholder communication

## Code Example

```javascript
// Tiny cache helper for hot paths
const cache = new Map();
async function getCached(key, fetch){
  if (cache.has(key)) return cache.get(key);
  const val = await fetch();
  cache.set(key, val);
  return val;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure success if latency improvements reduce throughput?
- What would you change if a third-party dependency introduces higher error rates after caching is added?

## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to design lightweight governance frameworks for multi-team organizations with regional considerations, emphasizing practical artifacts, rituals, and measurable outcomes.

## Key Concepts

- Engineering governance
- Artifacts and rituals
- Metrics and experiments

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple guardrail filter: decide if a feature request should be evaluated against guardrails
function shouldGuardrailsApply(request) {
  const highImpactPatterns = [/auth|security|data/i];
  return highImpactPatterns.some((r) => r.test(request.description));
}
```
